Package: flickos-fleet
Architecture: all
# The owners whose commands and site files it uses (docs/design/flickos-fleet.md
# ADR-004, ADR-011): site defaults, apply-defaults, system settings as root.
Depends: python3,
         flickos-control (>= 1.73~),
         flickos-layouts (>= 1.87),
         flickos-settings (>= 1.59),
         flick-tiler (>= 1.13),
         flickos-welcome (>= 1.10),
         flickos-countme,
         systemd,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: keep FlickOS computers set up the way their organization chose
 The agent of FlickOS's service for organizations that look after many
 computers: schools, offices, internet cafes and PC refurbishers. It applies
 the organization's policy (layout and style, input and idle settings,
 updates, firewall, apps) through FlickOS's own commands, and owns no
 setting itself. It knows a fixed list of settings and never runs a command
 it is sent.
 .
 Nothing runs until the computer's administrator joins an organization.
 "flickos-fleet check FILE --dry-run" shows what a policy would change.
